# Code ownership and required review.
#
# The paths below are where a mistake becomes a security defect rather than a
# bug. They carry the controls that the rest of the system assumes are working:
# the authority boundary, the capability surface, and the corpus that proves
# both still hold.
#
# Replace @owner with the security reviewer or team, and enable "Require review
# from Code Owners" in branch protection for this file to have any effect.

* @owner

# --- The control plane -----------------------------------------------------
# Deterministic, LLM-free, and the reason a compromised model gains nothing.
# Policy rules, the capability matrix, the audit chain, injection containment,
# redaction, and the approval identity boundary all live here.
/src/security/ @owner

# --- The capability surface ------------------------------------------------
# Every tool an agent can reach, and the broker that authorises each call. A new
# tool here widens what a successful injection is worth.
/src/tools/ @owner

# --- Authority and routing -------------------------------------------------
# The deterministic router and the human-approval interrupt. Changes here can
# reorder or bypass the gate.
/src/agents/supervisor.py @owner
/src/graph.py @owner

# --- The trust boundary ----------------------------------------------------
# Every alert source terminates in parse_alert. Changes here decide what a
# hostile payload can be.
/src/ingest/ @owner

# --- Cross-run memory ------------------------------------------------------
# History feeds the policy engine. Changes here can open an injection channel
# into the one component that is not persuadable.
/src/memory/ @owner

# --- What the model is told ------------------------------------------------
# A prompt change is a behaviour change: severity guidance, what counts as
# benign, and the instruction to treat injected text as evidence all live in
# prose. Reviewed like the policy engine, because it decides similar things.
/src/prompts/ @owner

# --- Model provenance ------------------------------------------------------
# A tag is mutable; the digest pin is what makes a verdict attributable.
/src/model_provenance.py @owner

# --- The evidence that the controls work -----------------------------------
# Weakening the corpus weakens every claim made from it. In particular, the
# known-miss injection cases must not be quietly removed.
/evals/corpus/ @owner
/evals/runner.py @owner
/evals/baselines/ @owner

# --- The gate itself -------------------------------------------------------
# CI is what makes every control above enforced rather than aspirational.
/.github/workflows/ @owner

# --- Security documentation ------------------------------------------------
/SECURITY.md @owner
/docs/THREAT_MODEL.md @owner
/docs/CONTROLS.md @owner
